the most effective host discovery technique is through ICMP echo requests

-sn	       : disables port scanning
-Pn 	       : disables ICMP echo requests
-n	       : disables DNS resolution
-PE 	       : Performs the ping scan using ICMP echo requests
--packet trace : shows all packets sent and recieved
--reason       : displays the reason why NMAP prints a result
--disable-arp-ping : disables ARP ping requests
--top-ports=<num>  : scans the specified top ports that have been defined as most frequent
-p- : scans all ports
-p22-110 : scans all ports between 22 and 110
-p22, 110 : scans only ports 22 and 110
-F  : scans only top 100 most common ports
-sS : performs a TCP SYN-Scan
-sA : performs a TCP-ACK scan
-sU : performs a UDP scan
-sV : scans the discovered services for their version
-sC : perform a script scan with scripts categorised as 'default'
--script <script> : performs a script with the specified script
-O : OS detection
-A : performs OS detection, service detection, and traceroute scans
-D RND:5 : sets the numver of random decoys that will be used to scan the target
-e : Specifies the network interface to be used for the scan
-S 10.10.10.200 : specifies the source IP address for the scan
-g : specifies the port for the scan
--dns-server <ns> : DNS resolution is performed by using a specific name server
-oA <filename> : stores the results in all formats in a file
-oN <filename> : stores the results in normal format with the specified file
-oG <filename> : stores the results in a grepable format
-oX <filename> : stores the results in an XML file
--max-retries <num> : sets the number of retries
--stats-every=5s : displays the scans status every 5 seconds
-v/-vv : displays the verbose output of the scan (v- verbose, vv- very verbose)
--initial-rtt-timeout 50ms : sets the specified time value as initial RTT timeout
--max-rtt-timeout : sets the max RTT timeout
--min-rate 300 : sets the number of packets tat will be sent at the same time
-T <0-5> : specifies the specific timing template
--script <category> : sets the scan to run with a certain script category. categories are: auth, boradcast, brute, default, discovery, dos, exploit, external, fuzzer, intrusive, malware, safe, version, vuln.
to turn xml to html, use xsltproc

to update nmap scripts, do:
sudo nmap --script-updatedb
